# API Standards

All public HTTP APIs are versioned under **`/api/v1`**. Spring controllers use `@RequestMapping("/api/v1/...")`. Next.js/React clients call that prefix only (no unversioned `/api` resources).

## HTTP status

| Outcome | Status |
| --- | --- |
| Successful read or update with body | **200 OK** |
| Successful create | **201 Created** + `Location` when a new resource URI exists |
| Malformed request / Bean Validation | **400 Bad Request** |
| Semantically invalid state (illegal transition, not mutable) | **422 Unprocessable Entity** |
| Missing resource | **404 Not Found** |

Do not use **200** for creates. Do not use **500** for validation or domain-state errors the client can fix.

```java
// ❌ BAD — create implied 200
@PostMapping("/tickets")
public TicketResponse create(@RequestBody TicketCreateRequest req) { ... }

// ✅ GOOD
@PostMapping("/api/v1/tickets")
public ResponseEntity<TicketResponse> create(@Valid @RequestBody TicketCreateRequest req) {
    var created = ticketService.create(req);
    return ResponseEntity.created(URI.create("/api/v1/tickets/" + created.id())).body(created);
}
```

## Errors (RFC 7807)

- Every exception path returns Spring **`ProblemDetail`**.
- Include `type`, `title`, `status`, `detail`; add `instance` and field errors when useful.
- Validation → **400**. Business/state violations → **422**. Unknown id → **404**.

```json
{
  "type": "https://api.example.com/problems/illegal-ticket-state",
  "title": "Unprocessable Entity",
  "status": 422,
  "detail": "Cannot transition CLOSED to OPEN."
}
```

## Contract

- JSON: `camelCase`. Paths: plural nouns (`/api/v1/tickets`).
- Do not break `/api/v1` in place; incompatible changes go to `/api/v2`.
